{
    "$comment": [
        "Source media for the project reel. Raw recordings and screenshots are far",
        "too heavy to ship, so nothing here is committed — `npm run media` reduces",
        "each entry into public/media/<slug>/, which is.",
        "",
        "dir      — where the raw assets live. Relative paths resolve from the repo",
        "           root; absolute paths (another drive, your Pictures folder) work",
        "           just as well, so nothing has to be copied into the repo.",
        "clip     — the recording behind the plate. The whole walkthrough is used;",
        "           `start` trims a dead head and `duration` a dead tail, and",
        "           `poster` picks the frame the plate holds before it plays.",
        "           Omit `clip` and the project simply gets no video.",
        "stills   — optional. Listing files gives them meaningful output names and a",
        "           fixed order. Omit it and every image in `dir` is used, in name",
        "           order, named after its own filename. `at` pulls a still out of a",
        "           recording at that second instead of off an image file.",
        "",
        "Captions live beside each shot in src/lib/projects.ts — adding an image",
        "here does not put it on the site until it is referenced there."
    ],
